    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_718fd054",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts John McCain with text overlay 'claims to be pro-life' above and 'dies' below, implying a contradiction or hypocrisy in his public stance on abortion. This meme uses a juxtaposition of his political identity and his death to suggest that his pro-life claims were insincere or hypocritical. While not targeting a specific protected group with hate or abuse, it is harmful because it leverages a person's death to criticize their political beliefs, potentially inciting division or disrespect toward the deceased. The meme's intent is to ridicule or undermine McCain's credibility on a specific issue, using his mortality as a punchline, which can be seen as disrespectful and emotionally manipulative.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_1ea79215"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
